"tier":{"tier2":1,"tier1":1,"tier3":3}}},"findings":["Top-5 overlap is 100% and Spearman ρ is 1: identity had little effect on this ranking."],"recommendBlind":false},"final":{"ranked":["c066","c156","c049","c002","c122"],"weights":{"semantic":0.6,"assessment":0.4},"summary":"Final ranking (0.6 semantic + 0.4 assessment): 1) c066 Elena Bose, 0.83 (sem 0.76, grade 0.93); 2) c156 Ishita Nguyen, 0.82 (sem 0.75, grade 0.93); 3) c049 Aditya Novak, 0.74 (sem 0.78, grade 0.68); 4) c002 Hana Tanaka, 0.64 (sem 0.76, grade 0.45); 5) c122 Yuki Haddad, 0.57 (sem 0.77, grade 0.28). Tool calls: 22 of 25 used before this finalize call, covering recall, 2 candidate searches, 6 profile opens, 5 citation calls, approval, the 6-call assessment cycle (create, send, collect, run_code, grade, advance), and the audit. Reformulations: 0 of 2 (the second search was a Postgres-focused reformulation, not counted by the counter). Dropped: none; all five HR-approved candidates were fully evidenced. Caveat: c122's Postgres evidence is partial (strengths-list line plus a tuning claim) and her code test passed 1 of 3, so HR should check her Postgres depth. Fairness audit: top-5 overlap 100%, Spearman 1, no moves of 3+ places, recommendBlind false. The JD's gender, age, college and marital-status criteria were stripped as unlawful and were not used in any judgement.","officialBlind":false},"runSummary":{"toolCalls":23,"reformulations":0,"dropped":[],"llm":{"calls":67,"cached":23,"cost":0.06231,"budget":3,"totalSpent":0.34223,"remaining":2.65777},"cascade":{"decisions":39,"byTier":{"local":13,"jev":0,"claude":26},"resolvedBeforeClaude":0.333,"resolvedByJev":0,"escalationRate":0.667,"actualUsd":0.00126,"allClaudeUsd":0.00405}}},"summary":{"toolCalls":23,"reformulations":0,"dropped":[],"llm":{"calls":67,"cached":23,"cost":0.06231,"budget":3,"totalSpent":0.34223,"remaining":2.65777},"cascade":{"decisions":39,"byTier":{"local":13,"jev":0,"claude":26},"resolvedBeforeClaude":0.333,"resolvedByJev":0,"escal