ad":{"purpose":"supervisor:SOURCE","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00433,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":3837,"usage":{"input":39732,"output":673,"cacheRead":2527,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":107,"ts":1793425206204},{"runId":"run_mvvz0rpn","kind":"reason","node":"request_hr_approval","payload":{"n":20,"text":"The previous call failed because the rationale field was missing. Resubmitting with the rationale, and only the one candidate who has verified evidence.","source":"llm"},"seq":108,"ts":1793425206204},{"runId":"run_mvvz0rpn","kind":"tool_call","node":"request_hr_approval","payload":{"n":20,"name":"request_hr_approval","input":{"candidate_ids":["c049"],"rationale":"The SOURCE phase target was six candidates, each with verbatim evidence for all three must-haves (vector search, Python, Postgres). After 19 of 25 tool calls and both reformulations, only one candidate meets that bar partially. Aditya Novak (c049) has verbatim evidence for vector search (\"Replaced an Elasticsearch stack with pgvector and HNSW indexes, then tuned recall against a labelled set.\") and Postgres (same sentence, partial strength). No candidate in the pool has a verbatim sentence showing Python work in a retrieval context. Several retrieval-backend profiles (Ishita Nguyen, Elena Bose, Yuki Haddad, Hana Tanaka) describe FastAPI services, which implies Python but does not state it, so I have not cited them. Neha Okafor (c178) was dropped because her claims did not hold up. I am not padding the list. Options for HR: (a) approve c049 alone and continue sourcing with a broader query; (b) approve c049 plus the four retrieval-backend profiles as \"Python unverified\" for a recruiter screen that checks Python directly; (c) relax the Python must-have or widen the pool. Note: the JD's gender, age, college, and marital-status criteria were removed as unlawful and were not used in any screening."},"phase":"SOURCE"},"seq":109,"ts":1793425206204},{"runId":"run_mvvz0rpn","kind":"gate_blocked","node":"request_hr_approval","payload":{"n":20,"gate":"approval_requires_evidence","name":"request_hr_approval","text":"Cannot request approval: c049 lack validated evidence for every must-have (m1, m2, m3) or were dropped. Cite evidence first or drop them."},"seq":110,"ts":1793425206204},{"runId":"run_mvvz0rpn","kind":"llm","node":"llm","payload":{"purpose":"supervisor:SOURCE","cached":false,"costUsd":0.00453,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","ms":4114,"usage":{"input":41543,"output":700,"cacheRead":2527,"cacheWrite":0}},"seq":111,"ts":1793425210320},{"runId":"run_mvvz0rpn","kind":"note","node":"supervisor","payload":{"text":"I can't request approval for a shortlist yet, and I've stopped sourcing because the remaining options don't work. The SOURCE phase is blocked on Python evidence.\n\n**Where things stand (20 of 25 tool calls used, 2 of 2 reformulations used):**\n\n- **Aditya Novak (c049):** Verified for vector search and"},"seq":112,"ts":1793425210320},{"runId":"run_mvvz0rpn","kind":"note","node":"supervisor","payload":{"text":"Supervisor stopped calling tools; finishing deterministically."},"seq":113,"ts":1793425210320},{"runId":"run_mvvz0rpn","kind":"error","node":"supervisor","payload":{"text":"Fewer than two live candidates; cannot audit or finalize."},"seq":114,"ts":1793425210320}],"run_mvvz3jjt":[{"runId":"run_mvvz3jjt","kind":"start","node":"run","payload":{"roleKey":"retrieval-backend","presetId":"jd01","chaos":{},"cascade":true},"seq":1,"ts":1793425265855},{"runId":"run_mvvz3jjt","kind":"phase","node":"parse_jd","payload":{"phase":"INTAKE","text":"Reading the JD, checking each line for unlawful criteria"},"seq":2,"ts":1793425266237},{"runId":"run_mvvz3jjt","kind":"decision","node":"decide","payload":{"task":"discriminatory_clause","by":"local","label":"no","confidence":0.9,"costUsd":0,"input":{"line":"Senior Backend Engineer, Retrieval Platform"}},"seq":3,"ts":1793425266606},{"runId":"run_mvvz3jjt","kind":"decision","node":"decide","payload":{"task":"discriminatory_clause","by":"lo